# Icons

All inline UI icons live in `app/icons.js`. Do **not** write SVG path markup in HTML, CSS, or other JS files.

## Adding icons

1. Source paths from [Icônes — Google Material Icons (Round)](https://icones.js.org/collection/ic?s=info&variant=Round) or another licensed set the user approves.
2. Add the entry to `ICONS` in `app/icons.js` with correct `viewBox`, `markup`, and `attribution` when required.
3. Reference icons via `data-icon="id"` (optional `data-icon-class`) in HTML, or `createIcon()` / `mountIcon()` in JS.
4. Call `initIcons()` at page boot so `[data-icon]` elements are mounted.

## When you need a new icon

**Never guess or invent path `d` attributes.**

Instead:

1. Add a placeholder entry in `app/icons.js`:

```js
"my-icon": {
  viewBox: "0 0 24 24",
  markup: `<!-- PLACEHOLDER: user must add path from Icônes -->`,
  name: "round-???",
},
```

2. Wire `data-icon="my-icon"` (or `createIcon("my-icon")`) in the UI.
3. Tell the user which Icônes icon to copy and ask them to paste the path markup into the placeholder.

Brand images (`app/res/icon/`) stay as separate files — not inline icons.
